CLI.md §3.7, API.md F13, EVALUATION.md §13: a computed value shows the expression that built it,
then one `in <fn> (<file>:<line>)` line per frame of the stack that built it, innermost first.
-- args --
explain
size
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Twice n.
fn twice(n: Int) -> Int {
  return n * 2
}

/// Twice n plus one.
fn grow(n: Int) -> Int {
  return twice(n + 1)
}

/// Computed through two calls.
let size: Int = grow(4)
-- want --
[exit 0]
[stdout]
size = 10  Int
  computed  a/a.canon:6  n * 2
  in twice (a/a.canon:11)
  in grow (a/a.canon:15)
[stderr]
